  annotation "note_1771592752732_1", anchor: "Kaela set out a third cup without remark", text: "Three secret renegotiations of the Flipper Accord produced less functional cross-cultural resource-sharing than one merchant with a kettle and no questions.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592752732_2", anchor: "old memories released from the cracking ice — something witnessed that left her unable to register the destruction around her", text: "A penguin who lost the ability to read ice, seized by ice-memory escaping from a collapsing structure. She could no longer reach into the ice. The ice reached into her anyway. Whatever the Forum Floe had been remembering beneath seventeen years of aurora-silk commerce — it was not released *to* Kaela. She was simply the nearest vessel with the door already broken open. The Bastion Apex took her ability to knock. It did not seal the entrance.", type: :commentary, display: :full
